{
  "requirement": "{cite}`requirements.sdk.domain`\n\nThe {term}`requirements.sdk.application_domain` implements\n`trust_but_verify::Domain` to define its node-identity type. Its\nerror type is introduced in {cite}`requirements.sdk.errors`:\n\n```rust,ignore\npub trait Domain: Clone + Send + Sync {\n    // ...\n\n    /// The *identifier* identifies a particular node in the graph.\n    type NodeId: Clone + Eq + Send + Sync;\n\n    // ...\n}\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The subject `requirements.sdk.graph.domain_types` has one testable obligation. `Domain` must declare `type NodeId: Clone + Eq + Send + Sync`, and the application domain must implement it. The doc comment on the type is not testable.\n\n**Main test:** `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs#fn[domain_relationships_accept_opaque_types_and_send_only_errors]` covers the bounds in two ways.\n- **Loosened bound:** the generic helper `check_bounds<G: Domain>` calls `identity::<G::NodeId>()`, which requires `Clone + Eq + Send + Sync`. If any of those bounds were dropped from the trait, this would fail to compile.\n- **Added bound:** the fixture's `Identity` derives only `Clone, PartialEq, Eq`. It has no `Debug`, `Hash`, `Ord` or `Default`. If the trait gained an extra bound on `NodeId`, `impl Domain for Relationships` would fail to compile.\n- **Behaviour:** the test also exercises `node_content`, `load_evidence`, `store_evidence`, `node_path` and `outgoing_edges` with this identity type. It uses `==` on identities and checks that distinct identities give distinct paths.\n\n**Supporting tests:**\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/validation.rs#fn[enum_node_ids_distinguish_requirements_and_source_items_in_one_domain]` implements `Domain` with a structured enum `NodeId`. It asserts `assert_ne!` between variants and runs the node, edge and evidence operations.\n- `src/sdk.rs#mod[tests]/fn[habeas_paths_preserve_opaque_segments_and_separate_all_node_kinds]` and `src/authoring/sdk.rs#mod[tests]/fn[review_graph_delegates_unprepared_sources_and_paths_to_the_domain]` use the project's real `HabeasNode` as `NodeId`.\n- `src/sdk.rs#mod[tests]/fn[requirement_edges_and_input_freshness_use_the_sdk]`, together with the agent tests in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/tests.rs`, exercises the domain's node type end to end.\n\nI found no uncovered obligation and no missing `{test}` marking. The `Send`/`Sync` bounds are enforced at compile time. A negative check that a non-`Send` type is rejected is not required by the text.",
  "references": "2e0816c1915fe94d28b5451c052712a0824feb8e7d2babaf5a1c18a378452fcc",
